Hmm. Some people find them hard and others do well with them. Once you 
get them past the quest, they do pretty well.


> So, what are the top tips for the Tourist class - the essential advice
> for Tourist newbies?
> 

1. Use your pet early and often. I tend to write Elbereth liberally and 
let the pet(s) take care of the monsters until I can #chat with the 
priest to get the AC boost. Then kill wimpy monsters (e.g., gnomes) to 
start boosting your XL and skills.

2. Two large pets can clean out the Sokoban zoo with little or no help. 
The mimics on the top level are a problem and if you can sleep it (wand) 
or heal your pets, that's a bonus. My last ascension I tried to do 
Sokoban w/o gaining experience and killed a mimic by mistake but made it 
safely to Mine Town at XL:2.

3. As a tactical decision, wake up the wraiths in the quest home level 
and lure them to the main dungeon and kill them there if you need the XL 
boost (quest home is a graveyard).

4. As a tourist ascension kit, I prefer "Reflection, GDSM, and robe. 
Yes, the PYEC endows MR, but I prefer a reliable method. Other stuff 
works as well, so don't be too choosy.

5. Keep your wands charged with the PYEC, but stop after about 2 or 3 
recharges unless you don't mind losing a *lot* of HP to an explosion.

6. With stealth and a death wand, the quest nemesis goes down without 
any problem. The nemesis not too hard anyway, but I prefer no fight.

7. Gather and use daggers liberally. You can get expert in dagger and 
can #twoweapon as well. There are lots of other skills you can get at 
least basic in to help as well.

8. The tourist quest has plenty of stores - bring cash or a pet to get 
even more loot than usual.

Those are things that come to mind. If something isn't clear, don't 
hesitate to ask.
